  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_column_selection(data: dict, column_name: str) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Column Selection** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_column_selection(data: dict, column_name: str) -> list:\n    return pd.DataFrame(data)[column_name].tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
